*> Acceptance test, feature 002 (task T4806; docs/protocol/33 section 6 advance_weather, 4.2): with the rule false the weather timers and flags
*> stand still (WEATHER-CYCLE); with it true the rain timer counts down.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ACC-F2US2-WEATHER-RULE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RULE-NAME           PIC X(40) VALUE "advance_weather".
 01 WS-RULE-INDEX          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RULE-VALUE          BINARY-DOUBLE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "BR-RULE-FIND" USING WS-RULE-NAME WS-RULE-INDEX
     MOVE 0 TO WS-RULE-VALUE
     CALL "BR-RULE-SET" USING WS-RULE-INDEX WS-RULE-VALUE
     MOVE 0 TO CW-CLEAR-TIME
     MOVE 1000 TO CW-RAIN-TIME CW-THUNDER-TIME
     MOVE 0 TO CW-RAINING CW-THUNDERING
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 5
         CALL "WEATHER-CYCLE" USING WS-DIM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance advance_weather false: five cycles leave the rain timer at 1000" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1000 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE CW-RAIN-TIME TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-RULE-VALUE
     CALL "BR-RULE-SET" USING WS-RULE-INDEX WS-RULE-VALUE
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 5
         CALL "WEATHER-CYCLE" USING WS-DIM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance advance_weather true: five cycles count the rain timer down to 995" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 995 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE CW-RAIN-TIME TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM ACC-F2US2-WEATHER-RULE.

 COPY CORETEST.
